WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.430
What happens between a plan and the next move?

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:07.740
This is a recorded Minecraft prototype.

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:12.540
The game is on the left; the agent’s live decision panel is on the right.

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:17.940
The larger goal is to survive and progress.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:20.780
For now, the active plan is smaller:

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:24.100
equip a pickaxe and look for safely reachable stone.

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:29.980
But the known stone has no confirmed safe route.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:32.900
The plan warns against digging toward it.

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:36.060
In the game, movement continues among the trees.

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.070
The tactical plan updates.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:49.630
It now proposes moving away from the cramped workbench area to a

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:55.150
safe standing position, then reassessing nearby stone from fresh observations.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:04.580
Another revision turns toward the oak.

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:08.820
It calls for a safe route, the right tool, and a log within reach.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:12.510
Now a new checkpoint appears:

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:15.070
clear the flower, then recheck the stone.

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:19.630
A proposed step is not the same as an executed action.

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:24.080
This recording shows movement and changing decisions.

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:27.040
Learning and transfer still need testing.

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:34.420
The research challenge: turn useful experience into skills, then test what transfers.